  "notes": "Government back-office tool with a strong semantic color system: red (#9f2328 text on #fdf4f4/#fffafa) = disqualifying, amber (#7d5200 on #fffdf6/#fdf1d2, border #e3b953) = curable by deadline, green (#1d6b3e on #fbfdfb) = met. Mismatched field values in the record are colored red inline. Navy top bar carries a live deadline countdown in gold (#ffd98a). Status pills are 999px-radius outlined pills; panels 10px radius, inputs 6px, buttons 4px. Disposition panel has a thick red left rule. Cure actions are embedded as small white forms inside each failing check card ('To resolve:' guidance above a dashed divider). Deficiency notice tab renders a print-style paper document with bordered tables. Almost no shadows, no icons except ✓ glyphs in chips."
